<DocsLayout
  title="CLI Reference — PgDesigner PostgreSQL Tools"
  description="PgDesigner CLI reference: generate DDL, diff schemas, lint with 69 rules, merge models, generate test data, import .pdd/.dbs/.dm2/.sql. All flags and exit codes.">

<h2>Usage</h2>

<pre><code>pgdesigner [command] [flags] &lt;file&gt;</code></pre>

<p>Input files: <code>.pgd</code>, <code>.pdd</code>, <code>.dbs</code>, <code>.dm2</code>, <code>.sql</code>, or a PostgreSQL connection string. Flags may go before or after file names.</p>

<h2>Commands</h2>

<h3>pgdesigner (no command)</h3>

<p>Starts a local server on <code>127.0.0.1</code> and opens the visual editor in your default browser. Without a file it shows the Welcome Screen with sample schemas, recent files and import. The server stops when the browser tab closes.</p>

<pre><code>pgdesigner
pgdesigner schema.pgd
pgdesigner "postgres://localhost/mydb" -schema public -full
pgdesigner -read-only -port 8080 schema.pgd</code></pre>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>-port</code></td><td>random</td><td>Fixed port for the local server</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>-read-only</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Disable all write operations (the public demo runs in this mode)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>-app</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Open in Chrome/Chromium app mode, without the address bar</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>-schema</code></td><td>all</td><td>Schemas to read when opening a database (comma-separated)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>-full</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Also read views, functions, triggers and types when opening a database</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>generate</h3>

<p>Generate production-ready DDL from a schema file.</p>

<pre><code>pgdesigner generate schema.pgd
pgdesigner generate -o schema.sql schema.pgd</code></pre>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>-o</code></td><td>stdout</td><td>Output .sql file</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>diff</h3>

<p>Compare two schemas and generate ALTER SQL.</p>

<pre><code>pgdesigner diff old.pgd new.pgd
pgdesigner diff -f json old.pgd new.pgd
pgdesigner diff "postgres://localhost/mydb" schema.pgd -o migration.sql</code></pre>

<p>Either side can be a database: <code>diff &lt;dsn&gt; schema.pgd</code> gives the migration from the live database to the model.</p>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>-f</code></td><td><code>sql</code></td><td>Output format: <code>sql</code> or <code>json</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>-o</code></td><td>stdout</td><td>Output file; not written when there are no changes</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>lint</h3>

<p>Validate schema against 69 rules.</p>

<pre><code>pgdesigner lint schema.pgd
pgdesigner lint -f json schema.pgd
pgdesigner lint -s error schema.pgd
pgdesigner lint -fix schema.pgd</code></pre>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>-f</code></td><td><code>text</code></td><td>Output format: <code>text</code> or <code>json</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>-s</code></td><td><code>info</code></td><td>Minimum severity: <code>error</code>, <code>warning</code>, <code>info</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>-fix</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Auto-fix fixable issues and save</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>testdata</h3>

<p>Generate realistic INSERT statements.</p>

<pre><code>pgdesigner testdata schema.pgd
pgdesigner testdata -seed 42 -rows 100 schema.pgd
pgdesigner testdata -tables users,orders -o seed.sql schema.pgd</code></pre>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>-o</code></td><td>stdout</td><td>Output .sql file</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>-seed</code></td><td><code>0</code> (random)</td><td>Random seed for reproducibility</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>-rows</code></td><td><code>50</code></td><td>Rows per table</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>-tables</code></td><td>all</td><td>Comma-separated table names</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>convert</h3>

<p>Import from other formats or live database.</p>

<pre><code>pgdesigner convert schema.pdd -o project.pgd
pgdesigner convert schema.sql -o project.pgd
pgdesigner convert "postgres://localhost/mydb" -o project.pgd
pgdesigner convert "postgres://localhost/mydb" -schema public,billing -full</code></pre>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>-o</code></td><td>input name + .pgd</td><td>Output .pgd file; for a database, <code>&lt;dbname&gt;.pgd</code> in the current directory, which must not exist yet</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>-schema</code></td><td>all</td><td>Schemas to read from a database (comma-separated)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>-full</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Also read views, functions, triggers, extensions and types from a database</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p>Supported inputs: <code>.pdd</code> (MicroOLAP), <code>.dbs</code> (DbSchema), <code>.dm2</code> (Toad), <code>.sql</code> (pg_dump), PostgreSQL connection string.</p>

<h3>merge</h3>

<p>Merge two or more schemas into one <code>.pgd</code> — for example, combine models of separate services, or a model with a fresh import from the database. Inputs can be any supported format; files are merged left to right, and the later file wins on conflicts.</p>

<pre><code>pgdesigner merge -o merged.pgd base.pgd overlay.pgd
pgdesigner merge -o all.pgd -layout base users.pgd billing.sql orders.pdd</code></pre>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>-o</code></td><td><code>merged.pgd</code></td><td>Output .pgd file</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>-layout</code></td><td><code>both</code></td><td>Where diagram positions come from: <code>both</code>, <code>base</code> or <code>overlay</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>-name</code></td><td>last file's name</td><td>Project name of the result</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>version</h3>

<pre><code>pgdesigner version</code></pre>

<h2>Exit codes</h2>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th style="text-align:center">Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td style="text-align:center"><code>0</code></td><td>Success, including a diff with changes and lint with only warnings or info</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="text-align:center"><code>1</code></td><td>Lint errors found, missing arguments, file not found or parse error</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="text-align:center"><code>2</code></td><td>Unknown flag</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Platforms</h2>

<p>Single statically-linked binary. No runtime dependencies.</p>

<ul>
  <li>macOS amd64 + arm64 (signed, notarized)</li>
  <li>Linux amd64 + arm64</li>
  <li>Windows amd64 + arm64</li>
</ul>

